        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ex_Guidance" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#F7F8FA;strokeColor=#B3BAC5;fontColor=#172B4D;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;How the modules fit together for this domain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Customer journey:&lt;/b&gt; CloudFront (frontend_edge) serves a micro-frontend shell whose master manifests come from the manifest deployer (micro_frontend). Each user activity is its own micro-app backed by its own BFF (bff_service) and private table (dynamodb_table).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Event backbone:&lt;/b&gt; Tables publish business facts (CartCheckedOut, OrderPlaced, AddressUpdated) onto a single subsystem-scoped EventBridge bus (event_hub). Every consumer below the hub - Inventory Allocator, Order Fulfilment Saga and both ESG services - subscribes to the events it cares about and emits its own results back to the hub, so all collaboration stays asynchronous and there are no direct service-to-service calls.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Order Tracking BFF&lt;/b&gt; is read-only: its Order View Table is materialised from hub events (CQRS) rather than written by the BFF itself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;External integration:&lt;/b&gt; Payments Gateway and Shipping Gateway (esg_service) are anti-corruption boundaries around Stripe and DHL. Outbound API calls and inbound webhooks both go through the gateway.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Operations:&lt;/b&gt; Event Lake (event_lake) archives every fact for analytics and replay. Fault Monitor (fault_monitor) catches any fault-typed event for resubmission. Observability Baseline (observability_baseline) owns the alarms, SNS topic and dashboard; Regional Health Check (regional_health_check) decides whether Route 53 routes traffic to this region." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="1280" x="60" y="770" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
